exit 0
--- stdout
Usage:
  managed-machine catalog list [--json] [--no-refresh]
  managed-machine catalog resolve <name> [--json] [--no-refresh]

Introspect supported setup targets, catalog apps, aliases, kinds, commands,
and install/declined state without parsing --help or reading apps.json.

Alias resolution rules:
  setup <name>    accepts canonical catalog name, any catalog alias, Homebrew
                  cask token, wrapper script name (e.g. codex-cli -> codex),
                  or standalone setup script name, with or without a setup-
                  prefix.
  adopt <name>    accepts a signed-cask Homebrew token (canonical for adopt),
                  its catalog name, or any catalog alias (with or without a
                  setup- prefix).
  catalog resolve resolves any of the above forms and reports the canonical
                  entry plus whether setup and/or adopt accepts it.

Options:
  --json          emit structured JSON output and error envelopes
  --no-refresh    inspect the on-disk config checkout without fetching origin
--- stderr
--- probes
